{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466298",
      "title": "Errors & Completion",
      "lectureOrder": 499,
      "videoOrder": 458,
      "sourceHash": "73f2e2a84ab722db263eed34e2de799dc440cee2295b717fad23f031b3a5a39e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "-: Emitting new data is arguably",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 6.48,
          "en": "the most important thing observables do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.48,
          "end": 11.22,
          "en": "And in I'd say 99% of all cases when you subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.22,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "you'll pass that first argument where you are interested in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "the data you are getting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 17.76,
          "en": "Or maybe it's 90%",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.76,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "because there is one other important use case too",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "especially when we think about things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "like HTP requests and that is error handling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 29.37,
          "en": "This counter here can't fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.37,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "There is no error that could occur here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 36.03,
          "en": "but that's a different story if you're sending HTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.03,
          "end": 37.8,
          "en": "which we will later do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.8,
          "end": 40.23,
          "en": "So here, of course we can also fake an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.23,
          "end": 42.33,
          "en": "We can simply throw one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.33,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "and define our own condition when we want to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "Now to do that, we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 51.24,
          "en": "check if count is greater than three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.24,
          "end": 55.63,
          "en": "So if that occurs, then we'll first of all still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.49,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "emits that new data with the next method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "But then we'll also use the error method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "to throw a new error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "So here I'll create a new error object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "count is greater free,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "which of course is a horrible event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 73.28999999999999,
          "en": "that definitely is worth an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.28999999999999,
          "end": 74.37,
          "en": "Now if we do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "and I save everything, let's see what happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 82.02,
          "en": "It starts counting again and as soon as we exceed three",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.02,
          "end": 83.19,
          "en": "we get an error here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "We get our error that we defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 88.47,
          "en": "And you see that the observable now stops emitting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.47,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "It actually gives us four, which makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "because that's the last value it emits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "before this condition is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "But there are no other values emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 100.5,
          "en": "because whenever an observable throws an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.5,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "it cancels, it's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "It will not emit any error values, it dies so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "And therefore in that case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "you also don't need to unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 111.69,
          "en": "You still can unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.69,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "If you never get away, you'll not get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 118.08,
          "en": "But it's not necessary because, well, it was dead anyways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "but you might not have known that when you unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.27,
          "en": "So unsubscribing is not an issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.27,
          "end": 125.037,
          "en": "Now this is how you can throw your own errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.037,
          "end": 129.27,
          "en": "and of course it's more important to not just throw them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.27,
          "end": 131.1,
          "en": "that most of the time will be done for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 133.59,
          "en": "when you're using some built in angular functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.59,
          "end": 136.05,
          "en": "that can fail like HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 136.05,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "But it's important to know how to handle that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 142.65,
          "en": "And for that you can pass another argument to subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 142.65,
          "end": 144.72,
          "en": "Thus far, we pass the first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "which is this data function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "The second argument would be our function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "that gets called when an error occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 153.32999999999998,
          "en": "and will get the error as an argument there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 153.32999999999998,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "Now of course the simple thing we can do here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 157.74,
          "en": "that we log that error to the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.74,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "but obviously you could do way more than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 162.39,
          "en": "You could send it to your own backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 162.39,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "and store it in a database there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 168.6,
          "en": "You can show an error message and alert to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 171.54,
          "en": "Let's actually do that. Let's show an alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 171.54,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "And let's show the error message here in the alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 176.28,
          "en": "So that's what we're doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 176.28,
          "end": 178.65,
          "en": "We're logging it to the console, we're showing an alert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 180.72,
          "en": "and now it starts counting again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "And as soon as we exceed three, here you go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "Now we get our alert and you see we don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 188.97,
          "en": "that red error here on the right anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 188.97,
          "end": 191.22,
          "en": "Instead it's now a regular console log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 191.22,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "because that's what we're doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 194.43,
          "en": "So now we're handling that error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 194.43,
          "end": 196.713,
          "en": "and that of course is also an important part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 201.03,
          "en": "Now handling errors is nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 201.03,
          "end": 203.46,
          "en": "but what about completing the observable?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "I told you that throwing an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "actually cancels the observable and lets it die.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "But completing it is something different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 215.31,
          "en": "Completing can be a normal process in an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 215.31,
          "end": 218.28,
          "en": "Now our interval by default doesn't complete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "It will emit new values until the end of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 224.22,
          "en": "And HTTP request on the other hand, will complete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "It completes whenever a response by the server is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 230.49,
          "en": "And of course here when we're building our own observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "from the crowned up, we can also complete this manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 238.23,
          "en": "In the end, we are defining how our observable behaves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 238.23,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "Our event source is the set interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 243.18,
          "en": "we have wrapped in our observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 245.88,
          "en": "and the (indistinct) before we throw an error let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 245.88,
          "end": 247.56,
          "en": "We can also add a narrow condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 247.56,
          "end": 250.26,
          "en": "Say if count is equal to two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 250.26,
          "end": 253.86,
          "en": "well then we simply call observer complete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 253.86,
          "end": 256.21,
          "en": "And there you don't need to pass any arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 257.76,
          "end": 259.86,
          "en": "Now when you call complete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 262.89,
          "en": "the observable will really come to an halt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 264.63,
          "en": "and you can see the view. Now reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.63,
          "end": 269.22,
          "en": "It logs zero, it logs one, it logs two, and that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 269.22,
          "end": 270.42,
          "en": "Doesn't log anything else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 270.42,
          "end": 272.46,
          "en": "Doesn't reach our error condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 272.46,
          "end": 275.85,
          "en": "because we complete the observable before it gets there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 275.85,
          "end": 279.03,
          "en": "And that is important to understand and to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 279.03,
          "end": 281.82,
          "en": "whenever an observable completes, it really is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 281.82,
          "end": 284.52,
          "en": "There are no other values emitted thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 284.52,
          "end": 287.52,
          "en": "which kind of makes sense because well it completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 287.52,
          "end": 290.19,
          "en": "Now if you want to react to that completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 290.19,
          "end": 293.01,
          "en": "you can add a third argument to the subscribe method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 293.01,
          "end": 295.8,
          "en": "and that is your completion handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 295.8,
          "end": 298.14,
          "en": "It's a function that gets no arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 298.14,
          "end": 300.87,
          "en": "because completing doesn't pass any arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 300.87,
          "end": 301.92,
          "en": "and it's simply a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 301.92,
          "end": 303.63,
          "en": "where you can do some cleanup work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 303.63,
          "end": 305.61,
          "en": "or whatever you need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 305.61,
          "end": 308.46,
          "en": "And here I'll just log, completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 308.46,
          "end": 311.25,
          "en": "Also important, you don't need to unsubscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 311.25,
          "end": 314.1,
          "en": "if your observable did complete, but again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 314.1,
          "end": 316.71,
          "en": "you might not know that here in ngOnDestroy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 316.71,
          "end": 319.773,
          "en": "So you can still do that without getting errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 321.6,
          "end": 324.39,
          "en": "So if I reload now, we see our logs again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 327.153,
          "en": "and after the two we see completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 329.82,
          "en": "Now all the worth noting though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 329.82,
          "end": 331.74,
          "en": "and important to keep in mind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 331.74,
          "end": 333.69,
          "en": "you might think that complete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 333.69,
          "end": 335.55,
          "en": "so that complete function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 335.55,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "all the fires when you're getting an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 340.35,
          "en": "after all the observable does finish",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 340.35,
          "end": 342.75,
          "en": "after throwing an error, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 342.75,
          "end": 344.58,
          "en": "Well, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 344.58,
          "end": 347.7,
          "en": "If we change the complete condition here, temporarily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 347.7,
          "end": 351.72,
          "en": "to let's say four, and therefore this to five, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 351.72,
          "end": 355.62,
          "en": "and therefore, this will happen after this condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 355.62,
          "end": 357.72,
          "en": "which actually will throw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
